Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: use integrated qcom,snps-dwc3

Linux v7.3 already provides the integrated Qualcomm DWC3 glue binding and
driver.  The legacy qcom,dwc3 binding is marked deprecated and models the
wrapper and core as separate platform devices.

Move both SM8150 USB instances to the integrated node so one device owns the
core, QSCRATCH registers, PHYs and interrupts.  Keep the old labels as
aliases so existing board DTS files continue to compile.

The Realme X2 Pro has a USB 2.0 receptacle.  Select the UTMI pipe clock and
high-speed maximum in the board layer instead of probing the unused combo
PHY.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -3728,14 +3728,10 @@
 			qcom,bcm-voters = <&apps_bcm_voter>;
 		};
 
-		usb_1: usb@a6f8800 {
-			compatible = "qcom,sm8150-dwc3", "qcom,dwc3";
-			reg = <0 0x0a6f8800 0 0x400>;
+		usb_1: usb_1_dwc3: usb@a600000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sm8150-dwc3", "qcom,snps-dwc3";
+			reg = <0 0x0a600000 0 0xfc100>;
 			status = "disabled";
-			#address-cells = <2>;
-			#size-cells = <2>;
-			ranges;
-			dma-ranges;
 
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_CFG_NOC_USB3_PRIM_AXI_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB30_PRIM_MASTER_CLK>,
@@ -3754,12 +3750,14 @@
 					  <&gcc GCC_USB30_PRIM_MASTER_CLK>;
 			assigned-clock-rates = <19200000>, <200000000>;
 
-			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 130 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
